        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Why Persistence Matters\n\nMost AI interaction today is disposable.\n\nChats disappear.\nContext collapses.\nIdeas fragment.\nMeaning drifts.\n\nTwilite treats knowledge as something that should accumulate structurally over time.\n\nInstead of generating isolated outputs, humans and AI can continuously evolve:\n\n- the same graph\n- the same relationships\n- the same semantic terrain\n- the same evolving artifact\n\nThis allows cognition itself to become:\n\n- persistent\n- navigable\n- inspectable\n- collaborative\n- expandable\n\nThe graph becomes durable memory instead of temporary conversation.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "html": "",
        "svg": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1778699709394,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    }
